From 76cd68aebc6ebd3e108a0ad846580837dcd8ccec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:00:36 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Ad hoc: say who the others cannot see, and why

Two players saw each other in the host's list on the Network page, which
only needs the matchmaking port, and never in the game's lobby, where
everything goes through the relay port and only to players in the same
group. Nothing said which of those failed.

- The server counts each player's relay connections and datagrams (sent,
  received, sent to nobody) and logs a player who has been in a group for
  10 s with no relay connection (kRelayMissingMs).
- The client keeps why each connection failed ("refused", "no answer"...)
  and counts relay connections that never came up while the server
  answers; adhoc::relay_unreachable() is true once that has lasted 10 s in
  a group. The game then says over the screen that the others cannot see
  this player and which port the host opens (<prefix>_NO_ADHOC_NOTICE=1
  never does), and Status says the same with the relay's address, its
  links and the failures.
- The host's list names each player's room as the game does
  (GameProfile::adhoc_group_name; the profile guide says how), marks a
  player in a room with no relay connection "not seen by the others" with
  a sentence on the two ports, and says when everyone is alone in a
  different room.
- Save network log starts with the build and the game, a port's own lines
  (ui::add_network_log_lines), the settings, the hosted server's players
  (room, relay connections, datagrams), the router and discovery, and adds
  the relay's state to the client's.
- <prefix>_ADHOC_LOOPBACK=1 hosts on 127.0.0.1 alone, asks no router and
  turns local network discovery off (the Network page says so): copies on
  one computer then open nothing a firewall asks about.
- adhoc_tests --loopback (ctest portablekit_net_loopback_tests) runs the
  new checks, which listen on loopback alone: per-player counts with two
  rooms and a player with no relay connection, and a stand-in server whose
  relay port refuses, through to the saved log.

Tested on Windows: the loopback ad hoc tests and the framework tests
without the all-interface ad hoc suite (23 of 23, MSVC). With Dissidia 012
(clang release build), two copies on one PC with <prefix>_ADHOC_LOOPBACK:
players in different lobbies get the host's warning; a joiner that reaches
the server through a proxy passing only its first port sits in the same
lobby with no card on either side (the reported fault), and gets the
notice and the Status warning while the host's list marks it not seen;
both saved logs show it. Not run: the all-interface ad hoc suite (it
raises a firewall prompt), two machines, Linux.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
